.TH "notcurses\-input" "1" "v3.0.17" ""
.SH "نام (NAME)"
notcurses\-input \- Read and display input events
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
\f[B]notcurses\-input\f[R] [\f[B]\-v\f[R]] [\f[B]\-m\f[R]]
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
\f[B]notcurses\-input\f[R] reads from stdin and decodes the input to
stdout, including synthesized events and mouse events.
To exit, generate EOF (usually Ctrl+\[aq]d\[aq]).
.PP
Each event will be printed on a single line.
Leading that line is a series of modifier indicators:
.IP \[bu] 2
\[aq]A\[aq]/\[aq]a\[aq]: Alt was or was not pressed.
.IP \[bu] 2
\[aq]C\[aq]/\[aq]c\[aq]: Ctrl was or was not pressed.
.IP \[bu] 2
\[aq]S\[aq]/\[aq]s\[aq]: Shift was or was not pressed.
.IP \[bu] 2
\[aq]U\[aq]/\[aq]u\[aq]: Super was or was not pressed
.IP \[bu] 2
\[aq]M\[aq]/\[aq]m\[aq]: Meta was or was not pressed.
.IP \[bu] 2
\[aq]H\[aq]/\[aq]h\[aq]: Hyper was or was not pressed.
.IP \[bu] 2
\[aq]X\[aq]/\[aq]x\[aq]: CapsLock was or was not pressed.
.IP \[bu] 2
\[aq]#\[aq]/\[aq].\[aq]: NumLock was or was not pressed.
.IP \[bu] 2
\[aq]L\[aq]/\[aq]R\[aq]/\[aq]P\[aq]/\[aq]u\[aq]: Key was a release,
repeat, press, or of unknown type.
.PP
By default, mice events are enabled.
.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
\f[B]\-v\f[R]: Increase verbosity.
\f[B]\-m\f[R]: Inhibit mice events.
.SH "نکات (NOTES)"
Mouse events are only generated for button presses and releases, and for
movement while a button is held down.
.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
\f[B]tack(1)\f[R], \f[B]notcurses(3)\f[R], \f[B]notcurses_input(3)\f[R]
.SH "نویسندگان (AUTHORS)"
